# Absolute Imports

Always use absolute imports with path aliases instead of relative imports.

## Next.js (apps/web)

Use the `@/` alias configured in tsconfig.json:

```typescript
// ❌ BAD - relative imports
import { Button } from '../../../components/ui/button'
import { cn } from '../../lib/utils'

// ✅ GOOD - absolute imports with @ alias
import { Button } from '@/components/ui/button'
import { cn } from '@/lib/utils'
```

## NestJS (apps/api)

Use the `src/` path, `utils/` path, or other absolute paths like `lib/` or module-based imports:

```typescript
// ❌ BAD - relative imports
import { AppService } from '../../../app.service'
import { UserEntity } from '../../entities/user.entity'

// ✅ GOOD - absolute imports from src or other absolute paths like utils
import { AppService } from 'src/app.service'
import { UserEntity } from 'src/entities/user.entity'
```
